#!/usr/bin/env bash
# The user guide: `prefix a h` shows it in a popup; invoking the skill with
# `help` prints it. Human keys first, the agent-facing API last.
cat <<'GUIDE'
TMUX AGENT COCKPIT — USER GUIDE                      (prefix = your tmux prefix, e.g. C-b)

SESSIONS — moving around
  prefix s          pick a session from a list (arrows + Enter)
  prefix a t        tree of sessions → windows → panes, zoomed
  prefix ( / )      previous / next session
  prefix L          back to the last session you were in
  prefix d          detach (sessions keep running)
  From a shell (inside or outside tmux — never nests):
    tm              session for this directory (create or switch)
    tp [name]       fzf picker, attached sessions first; or go straight to <name>
    tn <name>       session with an explicit name
    tv [file]       directory session that opens nvim
    tw <branch>     new git worktree ../<repo>-<branch> + its session
    twd [-f]        remove this worktree + its session (-f discards changes)
    tms [name]      sessions on $TMS_HOST over SSH

AGENTS — just run them
  Run claude / codex / gemini / … (or an alias like ccl) in any pane; it is
  tracked automatically. Claude Code reports its own state through hooks, so
  working / blocked / done are exact; other agents are read from the screen.

  prefix a b        next BLOCKED agent (waiting on you: approval, question)
  prefix a e        next ERROR agent (crashed / non-zero exit)
  prefix a w        next WORKING agent
  prefix a i        next IDLE agent (also finished ones you have not looked at)
  prefix a f        next FINISHED agent
                    Press the same key again to cycle to the next one.
  prefix a d        dashboard: every agent, its state and why
  prefix a m        menu: new agent pane, worktree, resume, splits
  prefix a s        rescan statuses now
  prefix a h        this guide

  Status bar: add #(…/scripts/agent-status-summary) to your status-right.
  Your own keys (panes, splits, zoom, copy mode) are untouched.

SETTINGS (export before starting tmux, or rerun the installer)
  AGENT_NOTIFY=tmux|system|off      toast channel (default tmux)
  AGENT_NOTIFY_SOUND=on|off         sound; blocked/error beep twice
  AGENT_SHELL_FUNCS=off|on          installer: drop/restore tm, tp, …
  AGENT_CLAUDE_HOOKS=off|on         installer: drop/restore Claude status hooks
  AGENT_ADOPT=off                   stop auto-adopting agents found by process

FOR AGENTS — coordination API (scripts/, invoked by path)
  agent-list [--json]               registry + statuses
  agent-read <name> [--lines N]     read another pane
  agent-send <name> <text> | --keys Enter    type (no Enter) / press keys
  agent-run <name> <command>        send command + Enter
  agent-wait <name> --status done | --match <regex>
  agent-jump <state>                focus the next pane in a state
  agent-explain <name|pane>         why a pane has its status
  agent-pane [--agent k] [--cwd d] <name> <cmd>   scripted launch
  agent-worktree create|open|remove|list <branch>
  agent-resume [--dry-run] [<name> --session-id <id>]
GUIDE
